L.H.S.

sqrt {frac{{1 - costheta }}{{1 + costheta }}} times sqrt {frac{{cosectheta - cottheta }}{{cosectheta + cottheta }}} 

⇒ sqrt {frac{{( {1 - costheta } )( {1 + costheta } )}}{{( {1 + costheta } )( {1 + costheta } )}}} times sqrt {frac{{( {cosectheta - cottheta } )( {cosectheta - cottheta } )}}{{( {cosectheta + cottheta } )( {cosectheta - cottheta } )}}} 

⇒ sqrt {frac{{(1 - co{s²}theta }}{{{{( {1 + costheta } )}²}}}} times sqrt {frac{{{{( {cosectheta - cottheta } )}²}}}{{( {cose{c²}theta - co{t²}theta } )}}} 

⇒ sqrt {frac{{si{n²θ}}}{{{{( {1 + costheta } )}²}}}} times sqrt {frac{{{{( {cosectheta - cottheta } )}²}}}{1}} 

⇒ frac{{sintheta }}{{1 + costheta }} times frac{{cosectheta - cottheta }}{1}

⇒ frac{{sintheta }}{{1 + costheta }} times ( {(1)/({sintheta )} - frac{{costheta }}{{sintheta }}} )

⇒ frac{{sintheta }}{{1 + costheta }} times frac{{1 - costheta }}{{sintheta }}

⇒ frac{{1 - costheta }}{{1 + costheta }}

Comparing with R.H.S.

frac{{1 - costheta }}{{1 + costheta }} = frac{{1 - r}}{{1 + r}}

r = cosθ 

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/bff1cbc858453d8644f26f54149bf7e747321adb95d41886add798f515c274d4.png] 

in the second step we have not taken conjugate but simply multiplied by 1 whose value is ( 1 + cosθ )/( 1 + cosθ ).
